        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: супруг",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "супруг (suprúg) — \"a spouse, a husband\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "На приём она пришла с супругом. Na priyóm oná prishlá s suprúgom. She came to the reception with her husband."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Formal. The wife is супруга; the plural супруги means a married couple."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "супруг (suprúg) is inherited from Proto-Slavic sǫprǫgъ (EtymDB), built on sǫ- 'together' and a root usually glossed 'to harness', so spouses are a pair in one harness."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
